<title>UK: GOLF-ALFRED DUNHILL CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-ALFRED DUNHILL CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ST ANDREWS, Scotland 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of final</p>
<p>round-robin group matches in the Alfred Dunhill Cup team golf</p>
<p>championship on Saturday (prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Group three:</p>
<p>Wales beat Canada 2-1 (Welsh names first)</p>
<p>Mark Mouland 75 lost to Rick Gibson 71</p>
<p>Phillip Price 71 beat Jim Rutledge 72</p>
<p>Paul Affleck 70 beat Rick Todd 72</p>
<p>Group three:</p>
<p>3-South Africa beat 6-Ireland 2-1 (South African names</p>
<p>first)</p>
<p>Retief Goosen 70 beat Darren Clarke 70 at 19th</p>
<p>Ernie Els 71 lost to Paul McGinley 69</p>
<p>Wayne Westner 69 beat Padraig Harrington 70</p>
<p>Group three final standings (tabulated under played, won,</p>
<p>lost, games won, points):</p>
<p> South Africa     3  3  0  6  3</p>
<p> Ireland	    3  2  1  6  2</p>
<p> Wales		3  1  2  4  1</p>
<p> Canada	     3  0  3  2  0</p>
<p>South Africa qualify for semifinals</p>
<p>Group one:</p>
<p>1-United States beat 8-Spain 3-0</p>
<p>Mark O'Meara 67 beat Miguel Angel Jimenez 68</p>
<p>Steve Stricker 70 beat Diego Borrego 74</p>
<p>Phil Mickelson 66 beat Ignacio Garrido 77</p>
<p>Group one:</p>
<p>Italy beat England 2-1 (Italian names first)</p>
<p>Costantino Rocca 72 beat Lee Westwood 74</p>
<p>Silvio Grappasonni 68 beat Jonathan Lomas 69</p>
<p>Emanuele Canonica 76 lost to Barry Lane 74</p>
<p>Group one final standings:</p>
<p> United States   3  3  0  7  3</p>
<p> England	   3  1  2  5  1</p>
<p> Italy	     3  1  2  4  1</p>
<p> Spain	     3  1  2  2  1</p>
<p>United States qualify for the semifinals</p>
<p>Group two:</p>
<p>4-Zimbabwe beat 5-Scotland 2-1 (Zimbabwe names first)</p>
<p>Tony Johnstone 70 beat Andrew Coltart 72</p>
<p>Mark McNulty 69 beat Colin Montgomerie 70</p>
<p>Nick Price 76 lost to Raymond Russell 72</p>
<p>Group two:</p>
<p>Sweden beat India 3-0</p>
<p>Patrik Sjoland 68 beat Jeev Singh 74</p>
<p>Peter Hedblom 69 beat Gaurav Ghei 72</p>
<p>Jarmo Sandelin 72 beat Ali Sher 73</p>
<p>Group two final standings:</p>
<p> Sweden     3  3  0  8  3</p>
<p> Zimbabwe   3  2  1  4  2</p>
<p> India	3  1  2  3  1</p>
<p> Scotland   3  0  3  3  0</p>
<p>Sweden qualify for semifinals</p>
<p>Group four:</p>
<p>7-New Zealand beat 2-Australia 3-0</p>
<p>Grand Waite 69 beat Wayne Riley 76</p>
<p>Greg Turner 69 beat Steve Elkington 73</p>
<p>Frank Nobilo 66 beat Greg Norman 68</p>
<p>Group four:</p>
<p>Germany beat Japan 2-1 (German names first)</p>
<p>Sven Struever 70 beat Naomichi &quot;Joe&quot; Ozaki 72</p>
<p>Thomas Goegele 71 beat Hajime Meshiai 77</p>
<p>Heinz-Peter Thuel 74 lost to Kazuhiro Takami 73</p>
<p>Group four final standings:</p>
<p>New Zealand    3  2  1  6  2</p>
<p> Australia	3  2  1  5  2</p>
<p> Japan	    3  1  2  4  1</p>
<p> Germany	  3  1  2  3  1</p>
<p>Sunday's semifinal line-up:</p>
<p>United States v Sweden</p>
<p>South Africa  v New Zealand</p>
<p>Tee-off times for Sunday's semifinals (times GMT)</p>
<p>United States v Sweden</p>
<p>0715  O'Meara v Hedblom</p>
<p>0725  Stricker v Sjoland</p>
<p>0735  Mickelson v Sandelin</p>
<p>South Africa v New Zealand</p>
<p>0745  Westner v Waite</p>
<p>0755  Goosen v Turner</p>
<p>0805  Els v Nobilo</p>
<p>The final will begin at 1230 GMT</p>
</text>
